IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap6-s2026`

-- TESTS for snap6-s2026.l4 (section 2026, Research, demonstration, and evaluations).
-- Every expected value is written here from the text quoted above the assertion, before the module was run.
-- JUST FALSE = "the text says no in its own words"; NOTHING = "not covered"; JUST TRUE = "the text says yes".


§ `Tests of section 2026`

§§ `(a) Contracts or grants; issuance of aggregate allotments`
-- src:2394 | (1) The Secretary may enter into contracts with or make grants to public or private organizations or agencies under this section to undertake research that will help improve the administration and effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in delivering nutrition-related benefits. The waiver authority of the Secretary under subsection (b) shall extend to all contracts and grants under this section.
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(1) the waiver authority of subsection (b) extends to the instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(1) the waiver authority of subsection (b) extends to the instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2395 | (2) The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months’ benefits. The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
-- "not more than two State agencies".
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the number of State agencies permitted is within the limit` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the number of State agencies permitted is within the limit` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the number of State agencies permitted is within the limit` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the number of State agencies permitted is within the limit` 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the inputs, in order: the household's monthly benefits; chooses to receive; the aggregate allotment; months covered.
-- Benefits of $20 or less, at their option, an aggregate not over $60 and not over 3 months.
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 20 TRUE 60 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 0 TRUE 0 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- over $60, or over 3 months: the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 20 TRUE 61 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 20 TRUE 60 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 25 TRUE 100 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- benefits over $20 (within the cap), or not at the household's option: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 21 TRUE 60 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` 10 FALSE 60 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- verification: "no household shall begin ... until it has complied".
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may begin to receive combined allotments` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may begin to receive combined allotments` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the household may begin to receive combined allotments` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the first aggregate allotment within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment was provided in time` TRUE 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment was provided in time` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment was provided in time` TRUE 41 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment was provided in time` FALSE 99 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b) Pilot projects`
-- src:2398 | (A) The Secretary may conduct on a trial basis, in one or more areas of the United States, pilot or experimental projects designed to test program changes that might increase the efficiency of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and improve the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to eligible households, and may waive any requirement of this chapter to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(A) the Secretary may waive the requirement of this chapter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(A) the Secretary may waive the requirement of this chapter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2400 | (i) Program goal.—
-- src:2401 | The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) unless—
-- src:2402 | (I) the project is consistent with the goal of the supplemental nutrition assistance program of providing food assistance to raise levels of nutrition among low-income individuals; and
-- src:2403 | (II) the project includes an evaluation to determine the effects of the project.
-- (i): consistent with the goal; includes an evaluation. Both met: the bar is lifted and nothing is granted.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary may conduct the project` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary may conduct the project` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary may conduct the project` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary may conduct the project` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2404 | (ii) Permissible projects.—
-- src:2405 | The Secretary may conduct a project under subparagraph (A) to—
-- src:2406 | (I) improve program administration;
-- src:2407 | (II) increase the self-sufficiency of supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients;
-- src:2408 | (III) test innovative welfare reform strategies; or
-- src:2409 | (IV) allow greater conformity with the rules of other programs than would be allowed but for this paragraph.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) the Secretary may conduct the project for the purpose` `s 2026 improve program administration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) the Secretary may conduct the project for the purpose` `s 2026 increase the self-sufficiency of supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) the Secretary may conduct the project for the purpose` `s 2026 test innovative welfare reform strategies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) the Secretary may conduct the project for the purpose` `s 2026 allow greater conformity with the rules of other programs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) the Secretary may conduct the project for the purpose` `s 2026 some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2411 | If the Secretary finds that a project under subparagraph (A) would reduce benefits by more than 20 percent for more than 5 percent of households in the area subject to the project (not including any household whose benefits are reduced due to a failure to comply with work or other conduct requirements), the project—
-- (iii): more than 5 percent of the households in the area.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) the restrictions apply to the project` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) the restrictions apply to the project` 5.01 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) the restrictions apply to the project` 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) the restrictions apply to the project` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2412 | (I) may not include more than 15 percent of the number of households in the State receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits; and
-- (I): not more than 15 percent of the State's households, for a project the restrictions apply to.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the project may include that share of the State's households` (JUST TRUE) 15 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the project may include that share of the State's households` (JUST TRUE) 15.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the project may include that share of the State's households` (JUST TRUE) 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the project may include that share of the State's households` (JUST FALSE) 50 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the project may include that share of the State's households` NOTHING 50 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2413 | (II) shall continue for not more than 5 years after the date of implementation, unless the Secretary approves an extension requested by the State agency at any time.
-- (II): not more than 5 years, unless the Secretary approves an extension the State agency requested.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the project may continue` (JUST TRUE) 5 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the project may continue` (JUST TRUE) 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the project may continue` (JUST TRUE) 6 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the project may continue` (JUST FALSE) 10 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the project may continue` NOTHING 10 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2415 | The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) that—
-- src:2416 | (I) involves the payment of the value of an allotment in the form of cash or otherwise providing benefits in a form not restricted to the purchase of food, unless the project was approved prior to August 22, 1996;
-- src:2417 | (II) has the effect of substantially transferring funds made available under this chapter to services or benefits provided primarily through another public assistance program, or using the funds for any purpose other than the purchase of food, program administration, or an employment or training program;
-- src:2418 | (III) is inconsistent with—
-- src:2419 | (aa) paragraphs (4) and (5) of section 2012(m) of this title;
-- src:2420 | (bb) the last sentence of section 2014(a) of this title, insofar as a waiver denies assistance to an otherwise eligible household or individual if the household or individual has not failed to comply with any work, behavioral, or other conduct requirement under this or another program;
-- src:2421 | (cc) section 2014(c)(2) of this title;
-- src:2422 | (dd) paragraph (2)(B), (4)(F)(i), or (4)(K) of section 2015(d) of this title;
-- src:2423 | (ee) section 2017(b) of this title;
-- src:2424 | (ff) section 2020(e)(2)(B) of this title;
-- src:2425 | (gg) the time standard under section 2020(e)(3) of this title;
-- src:2426 | (hh) subsection (a), (c), (g), (h)(1)(F), (h)(2), or (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title;
-- src:2427 | (ii) this paragraph; or
-- src:2428 | (jj) subsection (a)(1) or (g)(1) of section 2029 of this title;
-- src:2429 | (IV) modifies the operation of section 2014 of this title so as to have the effect of—
-- src:2430 | (aa) increasing the shelter deduction to households with no out-of-pocket housing costs or housing costs that consume a low percentage of the household’s income; or
-- src:2431 | (bb) absolving a State from acting with reasonable promptness on substantial reported changes in income or household size (except that this subclause shall not apply with regard to changes related to supplemental nutrition assistance program deductions);
-- src:2432 | (V) is not limited to a specific time period;
-- src:2433 | (VI) waives a provision of section 2035 of this title; or
-- src:2434 | (VII) waives a provision of section 2016(i) of this title.
-- (iv): the project's fields, in order: cash or not restricted to food; the date approved; transfers funds to another program; uses funds for another purpose;
-- the provisions it is inconsistent with; (IV)(aa) shelter deduction; (IV)(bb) reasonable promptness; (V) not limited in time; (VI) waives section 2035; (VII) waives section 2016(i).
-- None of (I) to (VII): the bar is not triggered and nothing is granted here.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (I) cash, not approved before August 22, 1996: the text says no; approved on August 21, 1996: not covered; on August 22, 1996: no.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF TRUE, JUST (Date 21 8 1996), FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF TRUE, JUST (Date 22 8 1996), FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF TRUE, JUST (Date 1 1 1990), FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a project approved before August 22, 1996 that is not cash: no (I) bar.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, JUST (Date 1 1 1990), FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (II), (III), (IV)(aa), (IV)(bb), (V), (VI), (VII), each alone.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST `s 2026 section 2017(b)`), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` (`s 2026 project` OF FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2419 | (aa) paragraphs (4) and (5) of section 2012(m) of this title;
-- src:2420 | (bb) the last sentence of section 2014(a) of this title, insofar as a waiver denies assistance to an otherwise eligible household or individual if the household or individual has not failed to comply with any work, behavioral, or other conduct requirement under this or another program;
-- src:2421 | (cc) section 2014(c)(2) of this title;
-- src:2422 | (dd) paragraph (2)(B), (4)(F)(i), or (4)(K) of section 2015(d) of this title;
-- src:2423 | (ee) section 2017(b) of this title;
-- src:2424 | (ff) section 2020(e)(2)(B) of this title;
-- src:2425 | (gg) the time standard under section 2020(e)(3) of this title;
-- src:2426 | (hh) subsection (a), (c), (g), (h)(1)(F), (h)(2), or (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title;
-- src:2427 | (ii) this paragraph; or
-- src:2428 | (jj) subsection (a)(1) or (g)(1) of section 2029 of this title;
-- (III): the ten provisions named, and any other is not on the list.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 paragraphs (4) and (5) of section 2012(m)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 the last sentence of section 2014(a), insofar as a waiver denies assistance to an otherwise eligible household or individual who has not failed to comply with any work, behavioral, or other conduct requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 section 2014(c)(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 paragraph (2)(B), (4)(F)(i), or (4)(K) of section 2015(d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 section 2017(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 section 2020(e)(2)(B)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 the time standard under section 2020(e)(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 subsection (a), (c), (g), (h)(1)(F), (h)(2), or (h)(3) of section 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 this paragraph` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 subsection (a)(1) or (g)(1) of section 2029` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` `s 2026 some other provision` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2436 | A pilot or experimental project may include projects involving the payment of the value of allotments or the average value of allotments by household size in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are age sixty-five or over or any of whose members are entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.] or are receiving assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household’s privacy, and the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards.
-- (v): the kind of project; all members 65 or over; any member on SSI; any member on part A assistance. Cash payments only for those households.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `s 2026 some other project` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2438 | Subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a) of this title, any pilot or experimental project implemented under this paragraph and operating as of October 1, 1981, involving the payment of the value of allotments in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are either age sixty-five or over or entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act shall be continued if the State so requests.
-- (vi): operating as of October 1, 1981 in the described way; the State requests; appropriations under section 2027(a).
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2440 | (i) No waiver or demonstration program shall be approved under this chapter after November 28, 1990, unless—
-- src:2441 | (I) any household whose food assistance is issued in a form other than EBT cards has its allotment increased to the extent necessary to compensate for any State or local sales tax that may be collected in all or part of the area covered by the demonstration project, the tax on purchases of food by any such household is waived, or the Secretary determines on the basis of information provided by the State agency that the increase is unnecessary on the basis of the limited nature of the items subject to the State or local sales tax; and
-- src:2442 | (II) the State agency conducting the demonstration project pays the cost of any increased allotments.
-- src:2443 | (ii) Clause (i) shall not apply if a waiver or demonstration project already provides a household with assistance that exceeds that which the household would otherwise be eligible to receive by more than the estimated amount of any sales tax on the purchases of food that would be collected from the household in the project area in which the household resides.
-- (C): the inputs, in order: the date of approval; a household's assistance in a form other than EBT cards; the allotment increased for the sales tax; the tax waived;
-- the Secretary determined the increase unnecessary; the State agency pays the cost; clause (ii) (assistance already exceeds the estimated tax).
-- After November 28, 1990, one way of compensating (or no household outside EBT) and the State paying: the bar is lifted, nothing is granted.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no way of compensating a household outside EBT, or the State agency does not pay: the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- on or before November 28, 1990: not covered; the day after: covered.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 28 11 1990) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 29 11 1990) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- clause (ii): clause (i) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` (Date 1 1 1991) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2446 | Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request for a waiver under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall provide a response that—
-- src:2447 | (I) approves the waiver request;
-- src:2448 | (II) denies the waiver request and describes any modification needed for approval of the waiver request;
-- src:2449 | (III) denies the waiver request and describes the grounds for the denial; or
-- src:2450 | (IV) requests clarification of the waiver request.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response is one the Secretary shall provide` `s 2026 approves the waiver request` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response is one the Secretary shall provide` `s 2026 denies the waiver request and describes any modification needed for approval` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response is one the Secretary shall provide` `s 2026 denies the waiver request and describes the grounds for the denial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response is one the Secretary shall provide` `s 2026 requests clarification of the waiver request` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response is one the Secretary shall provide` `s 2026 some other response` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2446 | Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request for a waiver under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall provide a response that—
-- "Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request": 60 days is in time, 61 is not.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` TRUE 60 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` TRUE 61 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` FALSE 61 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` FALSE 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` FALSE 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2452 | If the Secretary does not provide a response in accordance with clause (i), the waiver shall be considered approved, unless the approval is specifically prohibited by this chapter.
-- (ii): no response in accordance with clause (i), and the approval not specifically prohibited: considered approved.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) the waiver is considered approved` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) the waiver is considered approved` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) the waiver is considered approved` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) the waiver is considered approved` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2454 | On denial of a waiver request under clause (i)(III), the Secretary shall provide a copy of the waiver request and a description of the reasons for the denial to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate.
-- (iii): the Secretary denied under (i)(III); a copy and reasons to the House Committee; to the Senate Committee.
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary has given both Committees the copy and the reasons` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary has given both Committees the copy and the reasons` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary has given both Committees the copy and the reasons` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary has given both Committees the copy and the reasons` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary has given both Committees the copy and the reasons` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b)(2) Demonstration projects on employment and training`
-- src:2457 | (B) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Secretary may, as part of a project authorized under this paragraph, waive requirements under section 2015(d) of this title to permit a State to operate an employment and training program for supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients on the same terms and conditions under which the State operates its Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program for recipients of aid to families with dependent children under part F [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 681 et seq.). Any work experience program conducted as part of the project shall be conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of such Act (42 U.S.C. 682(f)).
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(2)(B) the Secretary may waive requirements under section 2015(d)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(b)(2)(B) the Secretary may waive requirements under section 2015(d)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
