§§ `(c) Evaluation measures; pilot programs for nutritional monitoring`
-- src:2466 | The Secretary shall develop and implement measures for evaluating, on an annual or more frequent basis, the effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in achieving its stated objectives, including, but not limited to, the program’s impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households, the program’s impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores, and the program’s relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence. Further, the Secretary shall, by way of making contracts with or grants to public or private organizations or agencies, implement pilot programs to test various means of measuring on a continuing basis the nutritional status of low income people, with special emphasis on people who are eligible for supplemental nutrition assistance, in order to develop minimum common criteria and methods for systematic nutrition monitoring that could be applied on a nationwide basis. The locations of the pilot programs shall be selected to provide a representative geographic and demographic cross-section of political subdivisions that reflect natural usage patterns of health and nutritional services and that contain high proportions of low income people. The Secretary shall report on the progress of these pilot programs on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982, to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate, together with such recommendations as the Secretary deems appropriate.
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the evaluations are made often enough` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the evaluations are made often enough` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the evaluations are made often enough` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the measures shall cover the impact` `s 2026 the program's impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the measures shall cover the impact` `s 2026 the program's impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the measures shall cover the impact` `s 2026 the program's relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the measures shall cover the impact` `s 2026 some other impact` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the locations of the pilot programs are selected as the text requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the locations of the pilot programs are selected as the text requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the locations of the pilot programs are selected as the text requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982" (fork FR-26-2): 1 July of each year from 1982.
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the date by which the progress report for the year is due` 1982 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 1982)
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the date by which the progress report for the year is due` 2000 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2000)
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the date by which the progress report for the year is due` 1981 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the Secretary submitted the progress report for the year in time` 1982 (JUST (Date 1 7 1982)) (Date 2 8 1982) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the Secretary submitted the progress report for the year in time` 1982 (JUST (Date 2 7 1982)) (Date 2 8 1982) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the Secretary submitted the progress report for the year in time` 1982 NOTHING (Date 2 7 1982) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the Secretary submitted the progress report for the year in time` 1982 NOTHING (Date 1 7 1982) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(c) the Secretary submitted the progress report for the year in time` 1981 (JUST (Date 1 7 1981)) (Date 2 8 1982) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(d) Employment initiatives program`
-- src:2472 | A State shall be eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection only if not less than 50 percent of the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of 1993 also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) during the summer of 1993.
-- (d)(1)(B): the households that received benefits in the summer of 1993; of those, the ones that also received part A benefits. "Not less than 50 percent".
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` 100 50 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` 100 49 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` 3 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` 3 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2470 | Subject to the other provisions of this subsection, a State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection.
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` 100 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` 100 49 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` 3 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` 3 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- src:2487 | A household shall be eligible to receive cash benefits under paragraph (2) if an adult member of the household—
-- src:2488 | (A) has worked in unsubsidized employment for not less than the preceding 90 days;
-- src:2489 | (B) has earned not less than $350 per month from the employment referred to in subparagraph (A) for not less than the preceding 90 days;
-- src:2490 | (C)
-- src:2491 | (i) is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.); or
-- src:2492 | (ii) was receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) at the time the member first received cash benefits under this subsection and is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income;
-- src:2493 | (D) is continuing to earn not less than $350 per month from the employment referred to in subparagraph (A); and
-- src:2494 | (E) elects to receive cash benefits in lieu of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits under this subsection.
-- (d)(3): the adult's fields, in order: days worked in unsubsidized employment; the least monthly earnings over those days; receiving part A benefits;
-- was receiving them when first receiving cash benefits; no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income; continuing monthly earnings; elects cash.
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 89, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 349, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 349, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2486 | (3) Eligibility
-- src:2487 | A household shall be eligible to receive cash benefits under paragraph (2) if an adult member of the household—
-- the household: an adult member who meets all five.
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the household is eligible to receive cash benefits` (LIST (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the household is eligible to receive cash benefits` (LIST (`s 2026 adult member` OF 10, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE), (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the household is eligible to receive cash benefits` (LIST (`s 2026 adult member` OF 10, 350, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE), (`s 2026 adult member` OF 90, 349, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 350, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(3) the household is eligible to receive cash benefits` EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2475 | A State that has elected to carry out an employment initiatives program under paragraph (1) may use amounts equal to the allotments that would otherwise be issued to a household under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, but for the operation of this subsection, to provide cash benefits in lieu of the allotments to the household if the household is eligible under paragraph (3).
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(A) the State may use amounts equal to the allotments to provide cash benefits to the household` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(A) the State may use amounts equal to the allotments to provide cash benefits to the household` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(A) the State may use amounts equal to the allotments to provide cash benefits to the household` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(A) the State may use amounts equal to the allotments to provide cash benefits to the household` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2477 | The Secretary shall pay to each State that has elected to carry out an employment initiatives program under paragraph (1) an amount equal to the value of the allotment that each household participating in the program in the State would be eligible to receive under this chapter but for the operation of this subsection.
-- (d)(2)(B): the value of the allotment each participating household would be eligible to receive, summed.
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(B) the amount the Secretary shall pay the State, in dollars` TRUE (LIST 100, 150, 50) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(B) the amount the Secretary shall pay the State, in dollars` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 2026(d)(2)(B) the amount the Secretary shall pay the State, in dollars` FALSE (LIST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2479 | For purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program (other than this subsection)—
-- src:2480 | (i) cash assistance under this subsection shall be considered to be an allotment; and
