§§ `(i) Testing resource accumulation`
-- src:2511 | The Secretary shall conduct, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary shall prescribe, for a period not to exceed 4 years, projects to test allowing not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate, to accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource) for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to improving the education, training, or employability (including self-employment) of household members, for the purchase of a home for the household, for a change of the household’s residence, or for making major repairs to the household’s home.
-- "for a period not to exceed 4 years" and "not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate".
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the projects are within the limits` 4 11000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the projects are within the limits` 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the projects are within the limits` 5 11000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the projects are within the limits` 4 11001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource)".
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` 10000 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` 9999 EQUALS 9999
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` 10001 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` 25000 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` `s 2026 improving the education, training, or employability, including self-employment, of household members` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` `s 2026 the purchase of a home for the household` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` `s 2026 a change of the household's residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` `s 2026 making major repairs to the household's home` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` `s 2026 some other purpose of expenditure` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(j) Demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking`
-- src:2513 | The Secretary shall use up to $4,000,000 of the funds provided in advance in appropriations Acts for projects authorized by this section to conduct demonstration projects in which State or local supplemental nutrition assistance program agencies test innovative ideas for working with State or local law enforcement agencies to investigate and prosecute benefit trafficking.
#ASSERT `s 2026(j) the funds used are within the limit` 4000000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(j) the funds used are within the limit` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(j) the funds used are within the limit` 4000001 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `(k) Pilot projects to evaluate health and nutrition promotion in the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
-- src:2517 | (A) of using the supplemental nutrition assistance program to improve the dietary and health status of households eligible for or participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:2518 | (B) to reduce overweight, obesity (including childhood obesity), and associated co-morbidities in the United States.
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(1) the pilot projects develop and test the methods the text requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(1) the pilot projects develop and test the methods the text requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(1) the pilot projects develop and test the methods the text requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2523 | To be eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant under this paragraph, an organization shall submit to the Secretary an application at such time, in such manner, and containing such information as the Secretary may require.
-- "To be eligible ..., an organization shall submit ... an application": not submitting is the text's no; submitting is necessary and grants nothing.
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(B) the organization is eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(B) the organization is eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2525 | Pilot projects shall be evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria that may include—
-- src:2526 | (i) identification of a low-income target audience that corresponds to individuals living in households with incomes at or below 185 percent of the poverty level;
-- src:2527 | (ii) incorporation of a scientifically based strategy that is designed to improve diet quality through more healthful food purchases, preparation, or consumption;
-- src:2528 | (iii) a commitment to a pilot project that allows for a rigorous outcome evaluation, including data collection;
-- src:2529 | (iv) strategies to improve the nutritional value of food served during school hours and during after-school hours;
-- src:2530 | (v) innovative ways to provide significant improvement to the health and wellness of children;
-- src:2531 | (vi) other criteria, as determined by the Secretary.
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 identification of a low-income target audience at or below 185 percent of the poverty level` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 incorporation of a scientifically based strategy designed to improve diet quality` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 a commitment to a pilot project that allows for a rigorous outcome evaluation, including data collection` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 strategies to improve the nutritional value of food served during school hours and after-school hours` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 innovative ways to provide significant improvement to the health and wellness of children` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 other criteria, as determined by the Secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` `s 2026 a criterion not listed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2526 | (i) identification of a low-income target audience that corresponds to individuals living in households with incomes at or below 185 percent of the poverty level;
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the individual is in the low-income target audience` 185 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the individual is in the low-income target audience` 184.99 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the individual is in the low-income target audience` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the individual is in the low-income target audience` 186 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2525 | Pilot projects shall be evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria that may include—
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the pilot projects are evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(C) the pilot projects are evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2533 | Funds provided under this paragraph shall not be used for any project that limits the use of benefits under this chapter.
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(D) the funds may be used for the project` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(2)(D) the funds may be used for the project` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2535 | Pilot projects carried out under paragraph (1) may include projects to determine whether healthier food purchases by and healthier diets among households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program result from projects that—
-- src:2536 | (A) increase the supplemental nutrition assistance purchasing power of the participating households by providing increased supplemental nutrition assistance program benefit allotments to the participating households;
-- src:2537 | (B) increase access to farmers [Footnote: 2 So in original. Probably should be “farmers’ ”.] markets by participating households through the electronic redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits at farmers’ markets;
-- src:2538 | (C) provide incentives to authorized supplemental nutrition assistance program retailers to increase the availability of healthy foods to participating households;
-- src:2539 | (D) subject authorized supplemental nutrition assistance program retailers to stricter retailer requirements with respect to carrying and stocking healthful foods;
-- src:2540 | (E) provide incentives at the point of purchase to encourage households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program to purchase fruits, vegetables, or other healthful foods; or
-- src:2541 | (F) provide to participating households integrated communication and education programs, including the provision of funding for a portion of a school-based nutrition coordinator to implement a broad nutrition action plan and parent nutrition education programs in elementary schools, separately or in combination with pilot projects carried out under subparagraphs (A) through (E).
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 increase the supplemental nutrition assistance purchasing power of the participating households` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 increase access to farmers' markets through the electronic redemption of benefits` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 provide incentives to authorized retailers to increase the availability of healthy foods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 subject authorized retailers to stricter requirements with respect to carrying and stocking healthful foods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 provide incentives at the point of purchase to purchase fruits, vegetables, or other healthful foods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 provide integrated communication and education programs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` `s 2026 some other kind of project` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2548 | The independent evaluation under subclause (I) shall use rigorous methodologies, particularly random assignment or other methods that are capable of producing scientifically valid information regarding which activities are effective.
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(4)(A)(i)(II) the independent evaluation uses the methodologies the text requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(k)(4)(A)(i)(II) the independent evaluation uses the methodologies the text requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2552 | Not later than 90 days after the last day of fiscal year 2009 and each fiscal year thereafter until the completion of the last evaluation under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that includes a description of—
-- (B): "Not later than 90 days after the last day of fiscal year 2009 and each fiscal year thereafter until the completion of the last evaluation".
-- The fiscal year ends on 30 September; 30 September plus 90 days is 29 December (fork FR-26-4).
