§§ `(n) Longitudinal data for research`
-- src:2599 | Subject to paragraphs (3) through (5), a State agency may, on approval by the Secretary, establish a longitudinal database that contains information about households and members of households that receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the State.
#ASSERT `s 2026(n)(1) the State agency may establish a longitudinal database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(n)(1) the State agency may establish a longitudinal database` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2601 | Each longitudinal database established under paragraph (1) shall be used solely to conduct research on participation in and the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including duration of participation in the program.
#ASSERT `s 2026(n)(2) the database may be used this way` `s 2026 research on participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including duration of participation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(n)(2) the database may be used this way` `s 2026 research on the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2026(n)(2) the database may be used this way` `s 2026 some other use` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2604 | (A) identify features that shall be standard across States such as database format to facilitate use of longitudinal databases established under paragraph (1) for research purposes;
-- src:2605 | (B) identify features of longitudinal databases established under paragraph (1) that may vary across States;
-- src:2606 | (C) identify a procedure for States operating longitudinal databases under paragraph (1) to use a unique identifier to provide relevant information on household members who receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the purpose of comparing participation data in multiple participating States over time while protecting participant privacy;
-- src:2607 | (D) establish the manner in which data security and privacy protections, as required by Federal law and consistent with other appropriate practices, shall be implemented and maintained;
-- src:2608 | (E) provide direction to State agencies on the responsibilities of and funding arrangements for State agencies and any State contractors (including entities providing technical assistance) relating to the establishment and operation of a longitudinal database;
-- src:2609 | (F) provide a description of the documentation that States shall submit to the Secretary prior to allowing researchers access to a longitudinal database;
-- src:2610 | (G) consult with other Federal research agencies, including the Bureau of the Census;
-- src:2611 | (H) consult with States that have already established databases used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection; and
-- src:2612 | (I) identify any other requirements determined appropriate by the Secretary.
-- (n)(3): the nine preparations (A) to (I), and whether the Secretary has approved State agencies. "Prior to the approval".
